# VIDEO-TO-TEXT MASTERPROMPT: "His Dad Kept Punching The Same Tree For An HOUR.."

## 1. SPECS & STYLE
* **Format:** 9:16 vertical Short (`1080x1920`), 67s (`00:00–01:07`).
* **Visuals:** 3D Minecraft machinima with warm shaders (sunlight, soft shadows, bloom) and rigid block rigs (no bent joints). Both indoor and outdoor sets are built in Minecraft blocks.
* **Typography & Cuts:** Fast 1–2s cuts across wide, medium, and macro angles. Center-screen bold uppercase blocky pixel font (`#FFFFFF`) with black outline (`#000000`), popping 1–3 words synced to narration. In-world dialogue uses dark translucent nametag boxes above speakers.
* **Audio:** Energetic young male narrator, punch/UI/shatter SFX, and uncredited cinematic BGM: muted synth/piano pulse (`00:00`) -> warm strings (`00:22`) -> silent/somber drop (`00:45`) -> soaring strings and arpeggios (`00:51–01:07`).

## 2. CHARACTERS & SETS
* **Dad:** Adult block rig; black hair, brown beard, wide open mouth, blue long-sleeve shirt with white chest stripe, yellow belt buckle, grey pants.
* **Tom:** Child block rig with floating `Tom` nametag; brown hair, blushing pink cheeks, orange hoodie with white drawstrings, blue pants, white shoes.
* **Set A (Forest):** Sunny flower forest, oak tree on dirt/grass, crafting table, chest, white background dome.
* **Set B (Bedroom):** Oak-plank room, green rug, left PC desk (black monitor, keyboard, wooden chair), back wooden bench under a 2x2 glass window (day/night sky).
* **Set C (Cottage):** Two-story oak-and-cobblestone house, pitched roof, window flower boxes, left soul lantern post, right potted red flower.

## 3. CHRONOLOGICAL TIMELINE
* **`00:00–00:09` Hook (Set A):** 1s cuts (profile, high-angle with crafting table, macro bark) as Dad clicks an oak tree, briefly cracking bark before it resets. *Captions:* `THIS DAD` / `PUNCHED` / `THE SAME` / `TREE` / `FOR AN HOUR` / `STARTED TO CRACK` / `WENT AWAY`.
* **`00:10–00:14` Reaction (Set B):** Tom laughs on the bench (`00:10–00:11`); Dad hunches stiffly at the PC desk (`00:12–00:14`). *Captions:* `SON TOM` / `COULDN'T STOP LAUGHING` / `NEVER PLAYED` / `VIDEO GAME`.
* **`00:15–00:21` Catch-22 (Set A):** Dad scratches his head under a pixel `?` (`00:15`), shrugs by the chest (`00:19`), and views a crafting table with a 3D wooden axe hovering over the 3x3 grid (`00:20–00:21`). *Captions:* `HOLD THE BUTTON` / `BREAK A BLOCK` / `MAKE AN AXE` / `NEEDS WOOD`.
* **`00:22–00:32` Refusal & Flashback (Set B):** Dad shakes his head refusing Tom's help at the PC (`00:22–00:25`). Bench flashback: Tom asks to play; Dad yawns, rubs his face, and slumps in guilt (`00:26–00:32`). *Captions:* `BY HIMSELF` / `FOR YEARS` / `TOO TIRED` / `FELT SO BAD`.
* **`00:33–00:37` Promise (Set B):** Starry night window; Dad speaks (`THIS WEEKEND,` / `I'LL BUILD YOU A HOUSE`) while Tom cheers arms up. *Captions:* `PROMISED TOM` / `ALL BY MYSELF`.
* **`00:38–00:46` Grind (Set B -> A):** Day sky; Dad sits at the PC (`00:38–00:39`), walks past the double chest to the tree (`00:40`), and repeats rapid-cut single-click punches with zero logs dropped. *Captions:* `SAT AT` / `FIRST TREE` / `1 HOUR LATER` / `SINGLE LOG`.
* **`00:47–00:50` Low Point (Set B -> A):** Music drops. Tom frowns on the bench (`00:47–00:48`); Dad slumps on the desk (`Sorry, Tom.`, `00:49`) and covers his face by the crafting table (`00:50`). *Captions:* `STOPPED LAUGHING` / `TOO OLD` / `THIS GAME`.
* **`00:51–00:55` Rescue (Set B):** Tom runs to the desk (`MINECRAFT` title screen visible on monitor at `00:52`), leaning beside Dad: `DAD!` / `DON'T CLICK IT.` / `JUST HOLD IT` / `JUST HOLD IT DOWN!`. *Captions:* `TOM RAN OVER` / `DON'T CLICK IT` / `HOLD IT DOWN`.
* **`00:56–01:07` Payoff & CTA (Set A -> C):** Continuous cracks shatter the oak log (`00:56–00:59`). Cut to Set C: Dad admires the cottage (`01:00–01:01`), poses smiling with Tom (`01:02–01:03`), and both turn to look at the house (`01:04–01:07`) as a white `Subscribe` pill clicks into `✓ Subscribed`. *Captions:* `HELD IT` / `3 SECONDS LATER` / `POPPED OUT` / `BUILT IT TOGETHER` / `SUBSCRIBE`.

## 4. WHY THIS SHORT WORKS (STORYTELLING BLUEPRINT)
* **The Hook (`00:00–00:14`):** Pairs an impossible gameplay premise (*punching one tree for an hour*) with instant emotional stakes (*keeping a promise*), immediately answers *how* (clicking resets cracks) to build viewer trust, and uses 1s camera cuts to hold attention.
* **The Middle (`00:15–00:50`):** Seals logical plot holes (no wood = no axe; refuses help), pivots from comedy to heart at `00:22` with warm strings and a starry-night guilt flashback, then cuts all music at `00:45` so the defeat lands emotionally.
* **The Ending Payoff (`00:51–01:07`):** Reverses roles as Tom teaches Dad, delivers tactile relief when the log finally pops, upgrades the goal (*building together* rather than solo), and places the Subscribe CTA over peak emotional satisfaction.